    },
    {
      "design": "r0B",
      "good": "Role labels and names remain intact, phone numbers fit on one line, and the week, role and engineer columns are visible at first. The shorter table makes the weekly groups easier to follow than in r0A.",
      "problems": "The viewport cuts through the phone column, so readers must scroll to use a number or read the notes. Notes still wrap into tall blocks, leaving substantial empty space in the other cells. Dates also wrap across several lines.",
      "cause": "The first three columns use 301px, leaving only 59px of the viewport for the 153px phone column. The 150px notes column provides 129px of text width, which produces up to seven lines in a cell. The 90px week column cannot hold the longest date range on one line."
    },
    {
      "design": "r0C",
      "good": "The week labels and dates form clear groups, names and phone numbers fit on one line, and wider notes give the rows a more compact, balanced rhythm.",
      "problems": "The first viewport cuts through the engineer column and shows neither phone numbers nor notes. The 403px overflow makes readers travel a long way sideways to reach the instructions.",
      "cause": "The 140px week, 99px role and 150px engineer columns together consume 389px. The 220px notes column reduces vertical wrapping but adds to the total width of 763px."
    }
